From 0856939e1d06a4f18c3b131991d371bc79d7a953 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alberto L <alberto_leon@seas.harvard.edu>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:15:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(controllers): optional DID-host allowlist for closed
 deployments

GATEWAY_ALLOWED_CONTROLLERS lists controller DIDs exactly. A deployment
whose DID hosts are closed (only the operator's own VTAs can publish a
DID there) can now also serve every did:webvh / did:web controller on
those hosts with GATEWAY_ALLOWED_CONTROLLER_HOSTS, so a new VTA does not
need a gateway redeploy. The host is part of the DID and resolution
fetches from it, so on a closed host "the DID lives here" means "the
operator created it". On an open host it admits anyone; the README says
so.

- an entry is an exact host or `*.` plus at least two labels, matching
  subdomains only (never the apex, never a look-alike such as
  evilexample.org); ports, paths, schemes and nested wildcards are
  refused and stop startup
- the host is read from did:webvh (segment 3) or did:web (segment 2),
  lower-cased, with a percent-encoded port dropped; other methods match
  only the exact list
- combining hosts with `*` is an error
- ControllerPolicy::Listed carries dids and hosts; admits_no_one()
  replaces the empty-set check in main; summary() names the hosts
- tests: host extraction, exact and wildcard matching, the apex and
  look-alike refusals, validation, admits_no_one

Signed-off-by: Alberto L <alberto_leon@seas.harvard.edu>
